use GCP services.

00:37:14.440 --> 00:37:16.770
And with that they brought
their own leadership team--

00:37:16.770 --> 00:37:19.515
their own CTO, their own
engineering leads and managers.

00:37:22.370 --> 00:37:25.610
Now, in some slides
back, we discussed

00:37:25.610 --> 00:37:28.223
that there was certain scenarios
where it would make sense

00:37:28.223 --> 00:37:30.140
where you would have
multiple billing accounts

00:37:30.140 --> 00:37:33.500
and multiple payment profiles,
and here's that example.

00:37:33.500 --> 00:37:36.740
Because Digital D0nut
functions in a US currency

00:37:36.740 --> 00:37:40.730
and has its own legal entity,
it has its own billing account

00:37:40.730 --> 00:37:41.750
and payments profile.

00:37:41.750 --> 00:37:43.700
But Digital Croissant
is functioning

00:37:43.700 --> 00:37:44.840
in a European market.

00:37:44.840 --> 00:37:47.720
They're going to be
having their own tax code

00:37:47.720 --> 00:37:50.040
and acting as its
own legal entity.

00:37:50.040 --> 00:37:52.040
They're going to be
receiving separate documents

00:37:52.040 --> 00:37:53.140
separate invoices.

00:37:53.140 --> 00:37:56.240
So it makes sense to have
this structure today.

00:37:56.240 --> 00:37:57.920
But as you grow as
an organization,

00:37:57.920 --> 00:38:00.020
as with every mergers
and acquisitions,

00:38:00.020 --> 00:38:03.170
we recommend that
eventually you start

00:38:03.170 --> 00:38:04.820
